  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The professions",
   "texto": [
    "To ask what does someone do: **Che lavoro fai?** (what work do you do?). With «Lei»: **Che lavoro fa?**",
    "It is answered in two ways: **Sono medico** (I am a doctor) or **Faccio il medico** (literally «I do the doctor.»). They're both normal.",
    "Many professions change in feminine: **infermiere** → **infermiera**, **cameriere** → **cameriera**, **studente** → **studentessa**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The verbs in -are",
   "texto": [
    "The verbs that end in **-are**, such as **lavorare** (work), are conjugated almost as in Spanish.",
    "Two differences: the «You» form ends in **-i** (**i**, not «lavoras») and «We» in **-iamo** (**iamo**).",
    "In the form of «They», the accent goes back: **LA-vo-ra-no**."
   ]
